%9Setting:%9

    colors_ansi_24bit (boolean; default: OFF, the Shellter default
    configuration sets ON)

%9Description:%9

    Sends 24-bit colours to the terminal where term_truecolor allows them.

    ON sends 24-bit colours for theme codes (%%Z and %%X followed by a hex
    colour), nick colours and mIRC colours 16-98 in their exact shades.
    OFF uses the nearest colour of the 256-colour palette instead.

    Whether the terminal shows 24-bit colours is decided by term_truecolor.

%9Examples:%9

    /SET colors_ansi_24bit on
    /SET colors_ansi_24bit off

%9See also:%9

    SET, TERM_TRUECOLOR
